    "和暦年齢メモ": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nenrin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "嘉永6年にペリーが浦賀へ来航しました。200年以上続いた鎖国が終わりに向かう転換点です。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Perry's fleet arrived at Uraga in Kaei 6 — the turning point at which more than two centuries of national seclusion began to end."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "土の兄（つち のえ）": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Elder earth (yang)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "土の弟（つち のと）": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Younger earth (yin)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "変更": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Edit"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "外観モード": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Appearance"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "大": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Large"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "大いに安らか": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Literally “great peace”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "大坂夏の陣で豊臣氏が滅び、戦国の世が終わりました。戦が絶えたことを「元和偃武」と呼びます。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The summer siege of Osaka destroyed the Toyotomi house and ended the age of warring states. The resulting peace is known as the Genna Enbu — “laying down of arms.”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "大飢饉（天保の飢饉）と、それに端を発する大塩平八郎の乱が起きました。幕府は天保の改革で立て直しを図りますが、失敗に終わります。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Tenpō famine struck, and with it the rebellion of Ōshio Heihachirō. The shogunate attempted the Tenpō Reforms in response, without success."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "女性": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Female"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "始まるまであと%lld年": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%lld years until it begins"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "存在しない日付です": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "That date does not exist"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "学年は4月に始まる": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Japanese school year starts in April"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "学校は4月に始まり、翌年3月に終わります。そのため、4月2日から翌年4月1日までに生まれた人が同じ学年になります。\n\n小学校は6年、中学校は3年、高校は3年で、6歳になった次の4月に小学校へ入学します。早生まれ（1月1日から4月1日生まれ）の人は、同じ西暦年に生まれた人より1学年上になる点が、年齢から学年を考えるときに間違えやすいところです。\n\n4月入学は明治期に会計年度に合わせて定められたもので、桜の季節と重なることから、入学式は春の風物詩になっています。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Japanese school year runs from April to the following March, so children born between 2 April and 1 April of the next year form one grade.\n\nElementary school lasts six years, junior high three and high school three; a child enters elementary school in the April after turning six. Those born between 1 January and 1 April — called hayaumare, “early born” — end up a grade above others born in the same calendar year, which is the easiest thing to get wrong when working a grade out from an age.\n\nThe April start was fixed in the Meiji period to match the fiscal year. Because it coincides with the cherry blossom, the entrance ceremony has become one of the images of spring in Japan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "宝永地震と、その49日後に起きた富士山の宝永噴火が記録されています。富士山の最後の噴火です。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Hōei earthquake is recorded here, along with the eruption of Mount Fuji 49 days later — the mountain's most recent eruption."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "家族・親戚・友人など、年齢を調べたい方を登録しておく名簿です。登録すると一覧がその方の生年月日を基準になり、各年に何歳になるかを確認できます。\n\n結婚記念日や開店日など、年ごとの区切りを数えたい日も「記念日」として登録できます。記念日を選ぶと、一覧の年齢の代わりに、その年で何周年にあたるかを表示します。\n\n【選ぶ】\n名前の行をタップすると、その方を基準にした一覧へ切り替わります。\n\n【追加】\n右上の＋を押し、「誕生日」か「記念日」を選んでから、名前（記念日は名称）と日付を入力して保存します。\n\n【変更】\n行の右端にある変更ボタンを押すと、内容を編集できます。行を左へスワイプして「変更」を選ぶこともできます。\n\n【削除】\n行を左へスワイプして「削除」を選びます。確認の後に削除され、取り消しはできません。\n\n【並べ替え】\n行を長押ししたまま上下へドラッグすると、好きな順序に並べ替えられます。並び順は保存され、追加や変更をしても崩れません。\n\n【周年の数え方】\n周年は月日を見ず、その年のうちは同じ数のままです。登録した年が0周年で、翌年から1周年になります。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A roster of people whose ages you want to look up — family, relatives, friends. Once someone is saved, the list uses their date of birth so you can see how old they are in each year.\n\nYou can also save a date you want to count in yearly milestones — a wedding anniversary, a shop's opening day — as an \"Anniversary\". Selecting one shows which anniversary falls in each year instead of an age.\n\n[Select]\nTap a name to switch the list to that person.\n\n[Add]\nTap + at the top right, choose \"Birthday\" or \"Anniversary\", then enter a name (a title for anniversaries) and a date, and save.\n\n[Edit]\nTap the edit button at the right of a row to change its details. You can also swipe the row left and choose Edit.\n\n[Delete]\nSwipe the row left and choose Delete. You will be asked to confirm, and deletion cannot be undone.\n\n[Reorder]\nPress and hold a row, then drag it up or down. The order is saved and is not disturbed when you add or edit someone.\n\n[How anniversaries are counted]\nThe count ignores the month and day — it stays the same for the whole year. The year you register is year 0, and the next year is the first anniversary."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "島原の乱と、それを受けたポルトガル船の来航禁止により、鎖国が完成しました。寛永通宝が広く流通します。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Shimabara rebellion, and the ban on Portuguese ships that followed it, completed the closing of the country. The Kan'ei Tsūhō coin came into wide circulation."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "幕府の体制が固まり、社会が安定した時期です。各地で新田開発が進みました。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The shogunate's institutions settled and society stabilised. New rice fields were developed across the country."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "干支": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "shouldTranslate": false
    },
    "干支は、十干（甲・乙・丙…の10種）と十二支（子・丑・寅…の12種）を順に組み合わせたものです。10と12の最小公倍数である60年で一巡し、61年目にまた同じ組み合わせへ戻ります。\n\n60年で生まれ年の干支に還ることを「還暦」といい、数え61歳を祝う習慣はここから来ています。\n\n「今年の干支は午年」のように十二支だけを指すことも多いのですが、暦の上での干支は十干と合わせた「丙午」のような形が本来の呼び方です。歴史上の出来事にも、壬申の乱や戊辰戦争のように干支の名が残っています。": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Eto pairs the ten heavenly stems (甲, 乙, 丙 …) with the twelve earthly branches (子, 丑, 寅 …) in order. Because 60 is the least common multiple of 10 and 12, the cycle takes 60 years to return to its starting point.\n\nReturning to the stem-branch of your birth year after 60 years is called kanreki, which is why the 61st year (by traditional count) is celebrated.\n\nIn everyday Japanese, “this year's eto” usually means the animal alone, but a full calendrical eto is the paired form, such as hinoeuma. Historical events carry these names too — the Jinshin War and the Boshin War are both named after the stem-branch year in which they were fought."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "年": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "shouldTranslate": false
    },
    "年と周年の早見表": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Years and anniversaries at a glance"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "年と年齢の早見表": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Year → age"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "年に付ける日本独自の名前": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
